  "name": "Get Concussed",
  "slug": "get-concussed",
  "teaser": "Adds the concussion and tinnitus effect to players when helmets receive headshots.",
  "thumbnail": "https://forge-static.sp-tarkov.com/mods/2448.jpeg",
  "downloads": 4886,
  "favourites_count": 0,
  "description": "<h3><strong>Showcase</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"youtube-lite\" data-video-id=\"XwLT6shnSDs\" data-embed-url=\"https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/XwLT6shnSDs?autoplay=1\"><img src=\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/XwLT6shnSDs/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"YouTube video thumbnail\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" /></div>\n<h3><strong>Overview</strong></h3>\n<p>Headshots will trigger the concussion/tinnitus effects if the bullet is blocked by helmet armor.</p>\n<p>Like Live EFT, tinnitus will only occur if you do not have a headset equipped.</p>\n<h3><strong>Install</strong></h3>\n<p>Extract directly into the SPT folder. The plugin can be located in BepInEx/plugins/.</p>\n<h3><strong>Background</strong></h3>\n<p>Concussions/tinnitus caused by gunshots to the helmet are currently not working. This mod restores the effect, for concussion lovers like myself.</p>\n<h3><strong>Configuration</strong></h3>\n<p>Hit F12 to configure concussion duration and concussion strength (default: 0.75 strength and 5 seconds duration), as well as turning tinnitus on/off.</p>\n",
